Package: plugin-hostd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: omx-clap-host
Suggests: mod-host
Description: run LV2 and CLAP plugins so that one crash cannot stop the show
 plugin-hostd keeps your effects and instruments running when one of them
 misbehaves. It gives a controller one mod-host socket and starts each plugin,
 or each named group of plugins, in a worker process of its own: mod-host for
 LV2, omx-clap-host for CLAP. If a plugin crashes, only its worker goes down
 and the daemon brings it back. Audio never passes through the daemon, so it
 adds no latency: every worker is a JACK client.
 .
 A format whose worker is not installed refuses its adds; the other format
 is unaffected. mod-host is not packaged by Debian: install it from source
 for LV2 plugins.

Package: plugin-hostd-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: C header to drive plugin-hostd from your own controller
 The C header that declares everything a controller needs to drive
 plugin-hostd: the verbs it adds to mod-host's protocol, error codes, feedback
 events and settings. Include it instead of copying the values, and pkg-config
 plugin-hostd gives the flags. The same declaration as JSON, for tools not
 written in C, ships in the plugin-hostd package.
